            </fr:date>
            <fr:anchor>1388</fr:anchor>
            <fr:addr type="user">sss-001U</fr:addr>
            <fr:route>sss-001U.xml</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Unambiguity as Unique Map into Codomain">Unambiguity as Unique Map into Codomain</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:p>A grammar <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is <fr:em>unambiguous</fr:em> if for all grammars <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex> and maps <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[e , e' : A \vdash  B]]></fr:tex> we have <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[e = e']]></fr:tex>.</fr:p>
            <fr:p>In a category with terminal objects, this is equivalent to unambiguity defined via subterminality.</fr:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="stevenschaefer.xml" title="Steven Schaefer" addr="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
